<article class="help-article p-4">
    <header class="help-article-header mb-4">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined help-article-icon">settings</span>
        <h1 class="help-article-title">Configurations</h1>
        <p class="help-article-lead">
            Configurations group parts of a model for store-specific or deployment-specific layouts.
        </p>
    </header>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Add a configuration</h2>
    <ol class="help-steps">
        <li><strong>Open the main menu</strong> and choose <em>Add Configuration</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Name it</strong> in the Inspector.</li>
        <li><strong>Save the project</strong> so the configuration is written into the model file.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        Use configurations when a model needs named groupings for generated stores or runtime behavior.
        Keep configuration names short and explicit so their purpose remains clear later.
    </p>
</article>
